SUMMARY:FYI: What’s happenin’
DESCRIPTION:Hendo Fun Friends\nUpcoming **music events** may be found here
 :\nhttps://www.facebook.com/hendolivemusic/\n\n**Assorted entertainment\, 
 festival & market events may be found here:**\nhttps://visithendersonville
 nc.org/calendar-of-events\n\n**Library programs** may be found here:\nhttp
 s://hendersonpl.libcal.com/\nSept 3\; 2 pm\; movie: Devil Wears Prada 2\n\
 n**Kiwanis Club Pancake Breakfast**\nSeptember 4 @ 7:00 am - 10:00 am\; $1
 0.00\nJoin the Kiwanis Club of Hendersonville for the official kick-off fo
 r the NC Apple Festival\, their annual Pancake Breakfast on September 4 fr
 om 7am to 10am at the First United Methodist Church of Hendersonville. Gue
 sts will enjoy pancakes\, eggs\, baked apples\, bacon\, coffee and juice! 
 Cost is $10 for ages 7 and older\; age 6 and under are free.\nhttps://visi
 thendersonvillenc.org/event/kiwanis-club-pancake-breakfast\n\n**80th Annua
 l NC Apple Festival**\; September 4 - September 7\nhttps://visithendersonv
 illenc.org/event/80th-annual-nc-apple-festival\nhttps://wlos.com/news/loca
 l/north-carolina-apple-festival-hendersonville-2026-parade-parking-road-cl
 osures?teaserSource=trending\n(not to be confused with the HFF event/ 7th 
 Avenue Apple Junction which is posted seperately.)\nNorth Carolina Apple F
 estival – Featuring The Buddy K Big Band (FREE Event)\nFri\; Sept 4th\; 
 6:30-8:30pm\, Stage in front of Old Courthouse\, 1 Historic Courthouse Squ
 are\, Hendersonville NC 28792\nYou will want to bring a chair as seating i
 s very limited.\n\n**Labor Day Harvest Festival at Grandad’s Apples**\; 
 September 4 - September 7\nhttps://visithendersonvillenc.org/event/labor-d
 ay-harvest-festival/2026-09-04\n\n**WNC Air Museum**\nSeptember 4 @ 10:00 
 am - 5:00 pm\; Free\nhelicopter rides\, aviation exhibits\, car shows\nhtt
 ps://visithendersonvillenc.org/event/labor-day-weekend-at-the-wnc-air-muse
 um/2026-09-04\n\n**Live Music Bingo at Souther Williams Vineyard**\nSeptem
 ber 4 @ 6:30 pm - 8:30 pm\; Free\nhttps://visithendersonvillenc.org/event/
 live-music-bingo-at-souther-williams-vineyard\n\nNorth Carolina Apple Fest
 ival (FREE Event)\nSat.\, September 5\; 11am-8:30pm\, Stage in front of Ol
 d Courthouse\, 1 Historic Courthouse Square\, Hendersonville NC 28792\nSch
 edule: 11am-Noon – The Stipe Brother\, 2-3pm – Elvis Impersonator\, 3:
 30-4:30pm – Group Project Band\,\n5:30-8:30pm – **The Big Throwback**.
  You will want to bring a chair as seating is very limited.s\n\n**Artist D
 emonstrations at Art MoB Studios**\nSeptember 5 - September 6\; Free\nArt 
 MoB Studios & Marketplace\; 124 4th Ave E\, Hendersonville\nhttps://visith
 endersonvillenc.org/event/artist-demonstrations-at-art-mob-studios\n\n**Br
 itish Car Club Show**\nSeptember 5\; 10:00 am - 3:00 pm\nLaurel Park Villa
 ge Shopping Center\; 1711 Brevard Road\, Hendersonville\nhttps://www.bccwn
 c.org/events/bccwnc-laurel-park-show-2026/\n\n**Grape Stomp**\n**September
  5**\nCelebrate harvest season at Burntshirt Vineyards’ Annual Grape Sto
 mp in Hendersonville. Join for one of our favorite traditions of the year 
 and experience a fun-filled day at the vineyard. Roll up your pants and ge
 t ready to stomp grapes\, enjoy live music\, explore the winery with winer
 y tours\, and sample award-winning Burntshirt wines.\nCome dressed as Lucy
  from the classic grape-stomping episode of I Love Lucy and enter our Lucy
  Costume Contest at 2:30 PM\nhttps://visithendersonvillenc.org/event/grape
 -stomp\n\n**Elks Lodge Apple Festival Breakfast**\nSeptember 6 @ 7:00 am -
  12:00 pm\; $8.00 – $12.00\nhttps://visithendersonvillenc.org/event/hend
 ersonville-elks-lodge-presents-apple-festival-breakfast\n\nSunday\, Septem
 ber 6\; Saints & Sinners\n2-5pm\, J&M Farms\, 3016 Chimney Rock Road\, Hen
 dersonville\nDance band\; Food truck available\nJ&M Farms has asst'd fruit
 s\, & canned goods\nThere is also a full service bar.\n\nSunday\, Septembe
 r 6\nNorth Carolina Apple Festival (FREE Event)\n4-8:30pm\, Stage in front
  of Old Courthouse\, 1 Historic Courthouse Square\, Hendersonville NC 2879
 2\nSchedule: 4-5pm – Free Flow Band\, 5:30-8:30pm – The Mighty Kicks.\
 nYou will want to bring a chair as seating is very limited.\n\nMonday\, Se
 ptember 7\nIt's 5 O'Clock Somewhere - Jimmy Buffet Cover Band\nNoon\, Okla
 waha Brewery\, 147 First Ave East\, Hendersonville\n\nMonday\, September 7
 \nThe Showboat Band\n2:30-5:30pm\, Point Lookout Vineyards 408 Appleola Ro
 ad\, Hendersonville\n\nWednesday\, September 9\nJason DeCristofaro's Jazz 
 Night (Each Wednesday)\n6-8pm\, Southern Appalachian Brewery\, 822 Locust 
 St\, Hendersonville\n\nThursday\, September 10\nSwing Social\n7-10:30pm\, 
 The School House\, 5495 Locust Hill Rd\, Travelers Rest SC 29690\n7-8pm - 
 East Coast Swing Dance Lesson and 8-10:30pm - Swing Social Dance.\nThis ve
 nue is temperature regulated and features gorgeous wooden floors. We play 
 a combination of pop\nand oldies\, and dance primarily east coast swing. C
 ost: $10 per person and includes the lesson.\n\n**Bullington Gardens Annua
 l Fall Plant Sale**\n**September 11** @ 9:00 am - 4:00 pm\; free\nBullingt
 on Gardens\; 95 Upper Red Oak Trail\, Hendersonville\nhttps://www.bullingt
 ongardens.org/eventsandclasses/fall-plant-sale-1\n\n**Jackson Park Bird Ou
 ting**\nSeptember 12 @ 8:00 am - 10:00 am\; Free\nhttps://visithendersonvi
 llenc.org/event/jackson-park-bird-outing/2026-09-12\n\n**2nd Annual Renais
 sance Festival**\nSeptember 12 @ 11:30 am @ Mills River Brewing\nHear Ye\,
  Hear Ye! Join the King & Queen for the 2nd Annual Renaissance Festival\, 
 a free family-friendly celebration filled with medieval entertainment and 
 adventure.\nEnjoy full-contact combat with Warriors of Ash\, live music\, 
 40+ vendors\, fire spinning by Unifire Theater\, belly dancing by Mystic M
 ountain Tribe\, Tomato Torment with Jester Adam\, giant turkey legs\, pret
 zels\, and other fair favorites. Guests can also meet the King & Queen thr
 oughout the day.\nThe festivities begin with the Royal Moonlit Masquerade 
 Ball on September 11\nhttps://visithendersonvillenc.org/event/2nd-annual-r
 enaissance-festival\n\n**Rockin’ on the Rock with Showboat Band**\nSepte
 mber 12 @ 5:00 pm\; Free\nEnjoy live music with musical offerings ranging 
 from jazz to country\, rockabilly\, pop\, rock and blues. Organized by the
  Friends of Laurel Park.\n\\*Rain date: September 13\nhttps://visithenders
 onvillenc.org/event/rockin-on-the-rock-with-showboat-band\n\nSaturday\, Se
 ptember 12\nBeach Night With DJ Dave Hadden (This event is open to the pub
 lic)\n6:15-10pm\, American Legion Post 77\, 216 4th Avenue West\, Henderso
 nville NC 28739\n6:15-7pm - Cy Miller and Joyce Anderson will teach a shag
  step. 7-10pm - Shag Dance.\nThe dance entry door is upstairs off of the u
 pper parking lot. Dave plays a great variety of music that\nincludes swing
 \, shag\, some cha-chas\, rhumbas and a line dance or two. Bring a partner
  or come solo.\nFull Bar and kitchen available with Free Parking in the up
 per lot. Cost: $7 per person (Cash only).\n\nThese are NOT hosted events a
 nd are posted for informational purposes only. Please make personal arrang
 ements to meetup with friends and family.\nIf you wish to attend and host 
 one of these events\, I will post the event as an individual happening. Ho
 sting only requires being focal point for others and making introductions.
  Simple!!
