SUMMARY:A Walk in the Park
DESCRIPTION:Hendo Fun Friends\n**A Walk in the Park\;**\n**This Week: 7th 
 Avenue Apple Junction**\nCelebrate the North Carolina Apple Festival with 
 a special tasting experience along **7th Avenue.** During Apple Junction\,
  visitors can explore participating businesses while sampling fresh local 
 apple varieties provided by Bright Branch Farm.\nFood-focused businesses m
 ay also feature apple-inspired treats\, drinks\, and specials throughout t
 he day. From crisp apple samples to seasonal flavors\, this event offers a
  delicious way to enjoy one of Hendersonville’s favorite traditions.\nht
 tps://visithendersonvillenc.org/event/7th-avenue-apple-junction\nSeptember
  5 @ 10:00 am - 2:00 pm\nVenue: 7th Avenue Historic District\; 650 Maple A
 ve\, H’vlle\ngordie's contact: curmudgeonhiker@gmail.com\n828.393.0297 (
 talk & text)
